      "path": "examples/manuscript.tex",
      "before": "\\documentclass{article}\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\section{A small revision example}\nLet \\(f:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R\\) be a differentiable function.\nFor \\(x\\in\\mathbb R\\), consider the increment\n\\[\n  f(x+h)-f(x).\n\\]\n\nThe first-order approximation is\n\\[\n  f(x+h)=f(x)+f'(x)h.\n\\]\n\nThis example contains two independent revision proposals.\n\n\\end{document}\n",
      "after": "\\documentclass{article}\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\section{A small revision example}\nLet \\(f:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R\\) be differentiable at \\(x\\).\nFor \\(x\\in\\mathbb R\\), consider the increment\n\\[\n  f(x+h)-f(x).\n\\]\n\nThe first-order approximation is\n\\[\n  f(x+h)=f(x)+f'(x)h+o(h),\\qquad h\\to0.\n\\]\n\nThis example contains two independent revision proposals.\n\n\\end{document}\n",
      "reason": "State the local differentiability assumption and include the missing remainder term.",
      "explanations": [
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "Only differentiability at the selected point x is needed for this local expansion."
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "text": "The first-order expression needs the remainder o(h); the equality is an asymptotic statement as h tends to zero."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
